# Extension Workflow

## After Modifying Extension Files

When ANY file in the `extension/` folder is modified:

1. **Always regenerate the distributable zip:**
   ```powershell
   Compress-Archive -Path "extension\*" -DestinationPath "public\crewforms-extension.zip" -Force
   ```

2. **Commit both the source files AND the zip together**

3. **Push to GitHub**

This ensures the downloadable extension at `/crewforms-extension.zip` always matches the source code.

## Extension File Structure

```
extension/
├── background/
│   └── service-worker.js    # Background service worker
├── content/
│   └── content-script.js    # Injected into web pages
├── sidepanel/
│   ├── index.html           # Side panel UI
│   ├── app.js               # Side panel logic
│   └── styles.css           # Side panel styles
├── icons/                   # Extension icons
└── manifest.json            # Extension manifest
```

## Testing Changes

After updating extension files:
1. Go to `chrome://extensions`
2. Click "Reload" on the CrewForms extension
3. Test the changes on a page with a mapping configured
